  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "No chapter describes its appearance.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court rank eights force open space over ordinary Hairy Foot Mountain after six rounds of attacks. The mountain looks small and poor, and nearby small and middle sized forces do not bother to occupy it. Heavenly Court research ties the opened land to the hairy man leader who once lived there and left an inheritance that gathers others’ failures into mortal failure Gu, which then condense into success dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        845
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "loc_hairy_foot_mountain",
        "race_hairy_men",
        "gu_failure_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The blessed land is perfectly enclosed and has no entrances at all.",
      "chapters": [
        845
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sealed-access-and-heavenly-court-use",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court can break it open by force, but doing so would destroy the wonders they want to keep, so they instead open it with coordinated rank eight work when the Refinement Path Convention nears its end. Bai Cang Shui complains that each opening costs heavy effort, and Lian Jiu Sheng says capturing the land outright would need both refinement path and rule path rank eights, which are rare.",
      "chapters": [
        845
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sealed-access-and-heavenly-court-use",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_refinement_path_convention",
        "char_bai_cang_shui",
        "char_lian_jiu_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Heaven Overseeing Tower Lord reports that Heavenly Court has pressed the land for thousands of years and still can take only thirty success dao marks when the inheritance accumulates to a thirty-six mark limit, leaving six for Refinement Path Convention participants that Heavenly Court cannot seize. After discovering the site, Heavenly Court used it as the foundation of the Central Continent Refinement Path Convention so the Infallible inheritance would accumulate mortal failure Gu faster, then applied the gathered success dao marks toward restoring fate Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        845
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sealed-access-and-heavenly-court-use",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_heaven_overseeing_tower_lord",
        "inh_infallible_inheritance",
        "gu_fate_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top six convention winners each receive success dao marks imprinted on the spot; one mark can at most cover rank six Immortal Gu refinement failure probability, and higher ranks need more.",
      "chapters": [
        847
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "sealed-access-and-heavenly-court-use",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Lang Ya land spirit guesses the hairy man racial inheritance is the Infallible inheritance, and places Infallible blessed land at Hairy Foot Mountain. Even after Heavenly Court found it, the court could not freely obtain it and relied on human path methods to extract part of its wealth; no Heavenly Court Gu Immortal had entered the secluded land, and nobody knew what the inside looked like. In Fang Yuan’s previous life, destroying Hairy Foot Mountain still left Infallible blessed land intact.",
      "chapters": [
        1769
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "limits-on-the-land",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lang_ya_land_spirit",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    }
  ],
